                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f6cac113-72cf-49c5-bb0e-4e9f81ccb80e",
                        "source_entry_id": "19e5d1df-06af-3347-bd19-7c01d156531b",
                        "source_sense_id": "94dd3a41-a6a1-36a3-baa9-fb3c63adb19c",
                        "target_lang_word": "suitor",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "suitor",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "83dac2ac-d90c-3207-b00d-e9cec04ab763",
                                        "entry_id": "28cb1188-460e-3968-8b81-4fb269cfcc48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who pursues someone, especially a woman, for a romantic relationship or marriage; a wooer; one who falls in love with or courts someone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2621bbf8-ec3f-4a0c-9df6-4f6c34a1657e",
                                                "sense_id": "83dac2ac-d90c-3207-b00d-e9cec04ab763",
                                                "text": "(Notice that \"Lysias\" begins from the realistic assumption that an attractive young man with many suitors will \"gratify\" one of them, the only question being which. Rightly or wrongly, he treats the question, \"Shall I at all?\" as already resolved.)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "546e2a88-a85f-3e0c-b969-6bca69dd0063",
                                        "entry_id": "28cb1188-460e-3968-8b81-4fb269cfcc48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or organization that expresses an interest in working with, or taking over, another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3022a34-92e5-4a6e-ab48-4c7b6da5842f",
                                                "sense_id": "546e2a88-a85f-3e0c-b969-6bca69dd0063",
                                                "text": "[…] and Mortimer asserted he had no shortage of suitors ready, willing, and able to make acquisition loans […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2eb4b99d-e94b-4ece-baf7-6d8d8a525000",
                                                "sense_id": "546e2a88-a85f-3e0c-b969-6bca69dd0063",
                                                "text": "The Betaville blog wrote earlier this week about market speculation that Adevinta was attracting takeover interest, without naming the suitors."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2e5448d-d0e6-3b0e-b322-beae8736754f",
                                        "entry_id": "28cb1188-460e-3968-8b81-4fb269cfcc48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A party to a suit or litigation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "19904872-cb01-37db-94fd-06feba9a9f9c",
                                        "entry_id": "28cb1188-460e-3968-8b81-4fb269cfcc48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who sues, petitions, solicits, or entreats; a petitioner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "suitor",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3633516a-133b-389f-b62c-daeaadf65433",
                                        "entry_id": "e2c57ad6-03b5-3d82-bd58-f257600a7f34",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To play the suitor; to woo; to make love."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cd6e04b0-739b-4429-9299-f0efc02f662f",
                        "source_entry_id": "19e5d1df-06af-3347-bd19-7c01d156531b",
                        "source_sense_id": "94dd3a41-a6a1-36a3-baa9-fb3c63adb19c",
                        "target_lang_word": "wooer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wooer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6902abfa-83e9-3e03-b426-ee3da762f646",
                                        "entry_id": "9e7ad886-55fe-37cc-9ab2-28314082311a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who woos or courts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd843a8c-b479-416e-8ae0-430a668e28c8",
                                                "sense_id": "6902abfa-83e9-3e03-b426-ee3da762f646",
                                                "text": "Penelope for her Vliſſes ſake, / Deuiz'd a VVeb her vvooers to deceaue: / in vvhich the vvorke that ſhe all day did make / the ſame at night ſhe did againe vnreaue, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7f5afe8-4b74-416a-ad02-17959b9366da",
                                                "sense_id": "6902abfa-83e9-3e03-b426-ee3da762f646",
                                                "text": "Whiles we shut the gate upon one wooer, another knocks at the door."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14b8557a-ecf0-4d7e-af20-665c586cd710",
                                                "sense_id": "6902abfa-83e9-3e03-b426-ee3da762f646",
                                                "text": "She wrote such a widow-like refusal when she went from me, as might not exclude hope in any other wooer; whatever it may do in Mr. Tony Harlowe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e51da18-07c5-4ab7-9209-ae1b3fe75497",
                                                "sense_id": "6902abfa-83e9-3e03-b426-ee3da762f646",
                                                "text": "Sally Leadbitter was vulgar-minded to the last degree; never easy unless her talk was of love and lovers; in her eyes it was an honour to have had a long list of wooers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff3b6039-418c-42b2-af6c-b152f2551a90",
                                                "sense_id": "6902abfa-83e9-3e03-b426-ee3da762f646",
                                                "text": "Never hold your heart in pain / For an evil-doer; / Never flip it down the lane / To a gifted wooer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9408a8f-9277-4b16-99c4-626f22abb202",
                                                "sense_id": "6902abfa-83e9-3e03-b426-ee3da762f646",
                                                "text": "She was, I think, the only girl I ever called on. I wasn’t much of a wooer. When I rang at her front door, her mother seemed taken aback. I should have been the dry cleaner’s messenger, picking up the blouses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
